-## Storage
+## Storage and signing key
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+The browser holds the member and expiry in a signed cookie. All web servers share `LARDER_SESSION_KEY`, supplied
+through deploy secrets, so any server can verify a cookie and a deploy preserves logins while the key stays the
+same. The [implementation](../../larder/sessions.py) defines the cookie encoding and signature; signing does not
+encrypt its contents.
+
+## Known limits
+
+- The server cannot revoke an individual member's session before its cookie expires. Wait for the
+  [session lifetime](#lifetime); the team accepted this limit for the pantry.
+- Rotating the signing key logs everyone out. Rotate it only between pickups to avoid interrupting members.
 
